# Kontakte-Apps (CardDAV)
contacts_dav_provider_label = Contacts (contacts)
contacts_carddav_title = Contacts on your phone and computer
contacts_carddav_intro = With CardDAV your address books appear directly in Apple Contacts, on the iPhone, in Thunderbird or on your Android phone. You maintain contacts wherever you already work.
contacts_carddav_point_sync = Changes sync in both directions, including custom labels and custom fields.
contacts_carddav_point_lists = Lists appear as groups in the app. A contact can be in several of them.
contacts_carddav_point_photos = Photos travel along: from the app to the backend and back.
contacts_carddav_point_password = The app gets its own app password, never your REDAXO password.
contacts_carddav_books_title = These address books appear in your app
contacts_carddav_books_intro = You see the address books your role allows you to maintain, provided they are offered to contact apps.
contacts_carddav_apple_note = Apple Contacts on the Mac only shows the first address book per account. iPhone, iPad, Thunderbird and DAVx⁵ show all of them. On the Mac one address book with several lists usually does the job.
contacts_carddav_no_perm = You lack the permission “DAV: connect devices and apps”. Please contact an administrator.
contacts_dav_book_create_denied = Address books are created in the REDAXO backend.
contacts_dav_book_delete_denied = Address books are deleted in the REDAXO backend.
contacts_dav_book_denied = No access to this address book.
contacts_dav_read_only = This app password is read-only.
contacts_dav_card_not_found = Contact not found.
contacts_dav_one_card = A resource must contain exactly one vCard.
contacts_dav_kind_change = A contact cannot become a list or vice versa.
contacts_vcard_unreadable = The vCard data cannot be read: {0}
contacts_vcard_empty = The file contains no vCard.

